1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:03,604
Japan. 2,000 years in 60 seconds.

2
00:00:03,644 --> 00:00:06,384
Over 2,000 years ago,
rice farming arrives,

3
00:00:06,424 --> 00:00:09,376
and villages grow
into small kingdoms.

4
00:00:09,416 --> 00:00:12,236
In 710, the court settles at Nara.

5
00:00:12,276 --> 00:00:15,074
Buddhism spreads,
and great temples rise.

6
00:00:15,114 --> 00:00:17,594
From 1185, samurai take power,

7
00:00:17,634 --> 00:00:20,374
and the emperor
reigns in name only.

8
00:00:20,414 --> 00:00:24,154
In 1603, the Tokugawa
clan takes over.

9
00:00:24,194 --> 00:00:27,451
Peace follows, and Japan
closes to most of the world.

10
00:00:27,491 --> 00:00:30,971
In 1853, American warships arrive.

11
00:00:31,011 --> 00:00:35,437
Within 15 years, the shogun falls,
and Japan modernises fast.

12
00:00:35,477 --> 00:00:38,077
Growth turns to empire, and war.

13
00:00:38,117 --> 00:00:42,741
In 1945, atomic bombs destroy
Hiroshima and Nagasaki.

14
00:00:42,781 --> 00:00:45,681
Japan rebuilds. In 1964,

15
00:00:45,721 --> 00:00:49,374
the bullet train opens,
and Tokyo hosts the Olympics.

16
00:00:49,414 --> 00:00:52,454
Today, over 120
million people live

17
00:00:52,494 --> 00:00:55,360
where ancient temples
meet neon cities.

18
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,780
Which country should
we print next?

